From caeebb67b5fcc3065de13885117a1aa27989c993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamal Saha <tamal@appscode.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 01:00:16 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Rebrand product name to "Postgres Enterprise by AppsCode"

Replace the product-name portion of the version string with "Postgres
Enterprise by AppsCode", leaving the numeric version exactly "18.6".
PG_VERSION, PACKAGE_VERSION, PG_VERSION_NUM, the PG_VERSION file in the
data directory and the server_version/server_version_num GUCs are all
byte-for-byte identical to upstream, so anything parsing \d+\.\d+ out of
version() or pg_config --version keeps working.

This is the entire AppsCode-specific diff on top of REL_18_6; it is meant
to be cherry-picked onto each new upstream point-release tag.

Version string surfaces changed:

  SELECT version()      configure.ac / meson.build PG_VERSION_STR
  startup log line      same (postmaster.c logs PG_VERSION_STR)
  pg_config --version   src/common/config_info.c
  <binary> --version    the "(PostgreSQL)" marker in src/bin, src/fe_utils,
                        src/interfaces, src/test and contrib

AC_INIT's PACKAGE argument becomes the new product name, so PACKAGE_NAME
and PACKAGE_STRING follow; TARNAME is pinned to "postgresql" so install
directories, pkg-config names and tarball naming are unaffected.
configure was regenerated with Autoconf 2.69, as configure.ac requires.

Two places parse a version string back out and needed adjusting, since
the product name now contains spaces:

  * pg_upgrade's get_bin_version() skipped a fixed two whitespace fields
    of "pg_ctl (PostgreSQL) VERSION".  It now scans back from the last
    space instead, which also keeps working against a stock PostgreSQL
    old cluster during a major-version upgrade.

  * PostgreSQL::Test::Version stripped a literal "(PostgreSQL) " marker.
    It now accepts either product name, so the TAP suite can still
    compare against stock PostgreSQL binaries.

Only the pgbench --version test asserted on the literal product name; its
expected pattern was updated rather than weakened.  No regression test
expected output needed changing.

Help text, documentation and translated message catalogs are deliberately
untouched; those are a separate, larger rebrand.

Signed-off-by: Tamal Saha <tamal@appscode.com>
